@FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5174

### 1. Registar a Alice -> 200 OK
POST {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2. Login da Alice -> Guarda o token globalmente
POST {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 3. Tentar listar transações SEM token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Accept: application/json

### 4. Criar transação para a Alice COM token -> 201 Created
POST {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Salário Alice",
  "amount": 2500.00,
  "type": "Income",
  "category": "Trabalho",
  "date": "2026-11-01"
}

### 5. Registar o Bob -> 200 OK
POST {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 6. Login do Bob -> Guarda o token do Bob
POST {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("bobToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 7. O Teste de Privacidade: O Bob lista transações
# Deve dar 200 OK com totalCount: 0 (o Bob NÃO vê a transação da Alice!)
GET {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. A Alice lista transações
# Deve dar 200 OK com totalCount: 1 e o "Salário Alice"
GET {{FinanceTrackerApi_HostAddress}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Accept: application/json